  "note": "Adstock and saturation act on impressions (*_impressions_000), not on spend. spend = impressions_000 * cpm. Saturation uses the SAME formula as pymc-marketing's LogisticSaturation: f(x) = L*(1-exp(-lam*x))/(1+exp(-lam*x)), with f(0)=0 exactly. Half-saturation point = ln(3)/lam (see effective_params.media.x50_half_saturation). FUNCTIONAL FORM: the media effect is MULTIPLICATIVE, not additive: sales_deterministic = base_combined * exp(media_log_multiplier), where media_log_multiplier is the sum of the saturation curves by channel (each with ceiling L_national * geo_multiplier, WITHOUT geo_size) attenuated by media_attenuation (formerly 'trade_factor', see trade_params). The L_national of each channel was rescaled (divided by ~22000, see metadata.l_national_rescale_constant) relative to an earlier additive version so that the media uplift would land in a reasonable order of magnitude. distribution_elasticity (in trade_params) IS the true elasticity of ACV on sales (gamma_true in effective_params.demand) -- before the media x distribution interaction was removed (MEDIA_GATED_BY_DISTRIBUTION=True) the effective gamma was not constant and exceeded distribution_elasticity. 'population' is fixed over time per geo (see geo_population), proportional to geo_size. See effective_params for the values ALREADY COMPOSED and ready to compare against a posterior -- do not rebuild L/gamma by hand from the input dictionaries (media_params_national_inputs, trade_params): use synthetic_data/true_params_reader.py."
